# GUI SKU only: XFCE desktop + display manager + the Calamares install-to-disk
# installer. Pulled on top of vacti-core.list.chroot. Headless SKU omits all of this.
xfce4
xfce4-terminal
# Human-operator desktop web browser. The engine's own Chromium (vacti-engine-chromium)
# is HEADLESS and path-coupled to the engine home (ms-playwright) for automated evidence
# capture - it is NOT a desktop-launchable browser. The GUI SKU therefore needs its own
# browser so the operator can reach the control plane and browse a target by hand.
# firefox-esr is Debian-main on both amd64 and arm64 (no Kali/third-party source needed).
firefox-esr
# Manual desktop screenshot tool for operator-captured evidence. Automated evidence is
# Playwright/Caido-driven (programmatic), but the operator has no manual SS tool on the
# desktop without this. xfce4-screenshooter integrates with the XFCE panel + hotkeys.
xfce4-screenshooter
# Whisker menu: the branded start-menu button (vacti radar-shield icon) wired by
# the skel xfce4-panel.xml in the branding layer.
xfce4-whiskermenu-plugin
lightdm
# GTK greeter: the LightDM greeter the brand greeter theme targets.
lightdm-gtk-greeter
network-manager-gnome
# --- PRE-LOGIN activation kiosk (vacti-activate, runs before LightDM) ---------
# Bare Xorg + a minimal kiosk WM so the kiosk renders without a desktop/compositor
# (works-everywhere: no GPU/compositor assumption).
xserver-xorg
xinit
openbox
# NetworkManager core (the -gnome frontend above pulls nm-connection-editor) +
# nmtui fallback. network-manager is the core daemon the kiosk drives.
network-manager
# Host-VPN frontends so the box can reach the control plane from behind a
# corporate VPN (HOST layer, distinct from the engine's per-engagement VpnProfile
# registry). NetworkManager VPN plugins + wireguard-tools / openconnect CLIs.
network-manager-openvpn-gnome
network-manager-openconnect-gnome
wireguard-tools
openconnect
# Premium pre-login kiosk: GTK4 + libadwaita Python app (vacti-kiosk). Chosen over
# a webkit webview (~45MB vs ~200MB, far more robust in a bare-X VM). yad + zenity
# remain the fail-soft fallback if GTK4/libadwaita ever fail to import.
python3-gi
gir1.2-gtk-4.0
gir1.2-adw-1
libadwaita-1-0
yad
zenity
# NOTE: polkit (polkitd) is pulled transitively by network-manager + lightdm, so
# the narrow 49-vacti-activate.rules applies without naming the package here
# (avoids an all-or-nothing live-build abort on a package-name mismatch).
# Plymouth: the graphical boot splash (vacti theme set by apply-branding.sh).
plymouth
plymouth-themes
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
